<doclang xmlns="https://www.doclang.ai/ns/v0" version="0.9"><!-- formula --><text><location value="64"/><location value="210"/><location value="436"/><location value="248"/>In summary, the model is described by equations (3.1)-(3.4). The aim is to solve them for the unknowns <formula>(p, q, r, s)</formula>. Using (3.6) and (3.5), we then obtain <formula>(u, v, w, s, \alpha)</formula>. The following section presents two example families of solutions to these equations.</text><!-- inline_key_value --><field_region><field_item><text><key>Invoice no.:</key> <value>2026-0042</value></text></field_item><field_item><text><key><bold>Issued</bold>:</key> <value>15 March 2026</value> (<value><italic>payable on receipt</italic></value>)</text></field_item></field_region><!-- inline_runs --><text>Water is H<subscript>2</subscript>O, and CO<subscript>2</subscript> is a gas.</text><text>Held on the 21<superscript>st</superscript> of June, see <italic>the agenda</italic>.</text><text>Some <bold>bold </bold>text with <code>code</code> inside.</text><!-- list_and_table --><list><ldiv/>First <bold>item</bold><ldiv/><italic>Second</italic> item</list><table><fcel/>a <bold>b</bold><fcel/>c<nl/></table><!-- kept_content --><text><content> Indented</content><content> by one space, a run of  two, and </content><bold>a line</bold><content>
break.</content></text><!-- paragraph --><text><location value="12"/><location value="40"/><location value="300"/><location value="58"/>See <italic>Table 2</italic> for the values of <formula>\beta</formula>.</text></doclang>
